(D2 -- minimal repro. LANGUAGE.md:5069 writes the second retired form as
 `see "lib" version "1.0" from "./path.so".` -- the library name in
 double quotes. That is not valid Vox syntax in this position: names are
 bare or 'single-quoted', never a string literal, so this hits a generic
 parse error instead of the "see of a .so" diagnostic the surrounding
 prose promises for all three retired forms (LIB-05b uses the correctly-
 shaped bare name and gets that diagnostic).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/libraries/D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: expected a name, found a string literal
   (compile error; also suggests `write \`mathkit\``, pointing out that strings are data while names are bare or 'single-quoted')
)
see "mathkit" version "1.0" from "./fixtures/libmathkit.so".

